---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Cohort"
  description="Cohort is an experimental study app from Project Cognify built to explore whether knowing that friends are studying nearby helps students stay focused."
>
  <h1>Cohort</h1>
  <p class="label">Our first research prototype</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Why We Built Cohort</h2>
    <p>
      One thing kept coming up across our interviews and survey responses:
      students said it was easier to stay on task when they knew other people
      were studying at the same time, even remotely. It lined up with what we
      were reading too, so we turned it into something testable.
    </p>
    <p class="question">
      Can just knowing your friends are studying alongside you make it easier
      to stay focused?
    </p>
    <p>Cohort is our attempt at answering that, as directly as we could build it.</p>

    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <p>
      You create or join a study session with three to six friends. Everyone
      in the session can see who's there and who's marked themselves as
      currently focusing. That's about it: no points, no streaks, nothing to
      compete over.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's still changing as we build it, so what's described here may not
      match what you see if you test the fall version. Whatever we learn
      between now and then will shape it.
    </p>

    <h2>What We're Actually Testing</h2>
    <p>
      Whether shared presence alone (without chat, without competition)
      does anything for focus. It might not. If it doesn't move the needle, we
      want to know that as much as we want to know if it does, because either
      answer tells us what to build next.
    </p>

    <h2>Current Status</h2>
    <p>
      Cohort is in active development. This fall we're inviting volunteer
      high school students to try it during the exam period, and we'll be
      watching how people actually use it against what we expected going in.
      Whatever we find, supportive or not, we'll write up on this site.
    </p>

    <p class="links">
      <span class="muted">GitHub: Coming soon</span>
      <span class="muted">Live Prototype: Coming soon</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .question {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
